<iscontent type="text/html" charset="UTF-8" compact="true"/>
<iscomment>
    Gameball widget fragment. Rendered ONLY through the Gameball-Widget remote
    include (see components/footer/pageFooter.isml), never with an isinclude
    template= : it is shopper-scoped, and SFCC page-cache keys do not include
    the customer, so inlining it would bake one shopper's name and email into a
    cached page and re-serve them to every subsequent visitor.

    CRITICAL - SECURITY BOUNDARY. The data-gameball-config attribute below is
    the security boundary of this entire feature. A double-quoted HTML
    attribute is the one context where the browser UNDOES the platform's
    encoding for us: ISML is expected to HTML-encode the interpolated value so
    nothing can break out of the attribute, and the HTML parser entity-decodes
    it again before getAttribute reads it, so the value round-trips byte for
    byte.

    UNVERIFIED - CHECK THIS FIRST. That ISML encodes an expression
    interpolated inside a double-quoted attribute has NOT been confirmed
    against a live instance; it was written with no sandbox and no Test API
    Key available. Arbitration risk R-5 designates exactly this the merge gate
    for this item, because gameballJson.toEmbeddableJson deliberately does NOT
    escape the double quote - the platform encoder is the only thing standing
    between the delimiters JSON.stringify emits and the end of this attribute.

    The 5-minute check: save the proof-of-concept first name from spec 01
    section 8.1 on a test customer, load any storefront page, View Source, and
    confirm this attribute contains &quot; and no literal double quote and no
    literal angle bracket. Two distinct ways it can fail. If the encoder
    escapes the angle brackets but not the double quote, the attribute
    truncates at the first delimiter, getAttribute returns just "{",
    JSON.parse throws and gameballWidget.js takes its silent return - a widget
    that never appears on any page, with nothing logged on either side and
    View Source as the only diagnostic. If the encoder does nothing at all,
    that raw quote closes the attribute and an event-handler attribute lands
    on the div - the stored XSS survives the fix, with toEmbeddableJson
    contributing nothing because no angle bracket is needed for that breakout.

    The one-token fallback if the check fails: wrap the same pdict value in an
    isprint tag inside the attribute value with its encoding set to
    htmldoublequote, which maps to
    dw.util.SecureEncoder.forHtmlInDoubleQuoteAttribute (confirmed present in
    the vendored dw-api-mock API surface). The exact spelling of that encoding
    token is itself UNVERIFIED - settle it in the same pass.

    The off encoding (encoding=off on an isprint tag) MUST NEVER be
    reintroduced in this file, or anywhere else in this cartridge. Grepping
    cartridges/ for that attribute-value pair and getting zero hits is the
    durable regression check for the stored XSS this template used to ship: a
    customer whose own first name closed the inline script element executed
    arbitrary HTML on every page of the storefront.

    The u003c / u003e / u0026 / u2028 / u2029 escapes visible in the attribute
    value come from gameballJson.toEmbeddableJson and are DEFENCE IN DEPTH
    only. Removing them would not reopen the hole; removing the platform's
    attribute encoder would. Their presence must not convince anyone that
    the off encoding is safe here.

    No isscript block here on purpose (I15): pdict.gameballWidget is assembled
    in controllers/Gameball.js, which is the only place a Site preference, a
    Service Credential or a customer identity is read.

    No iscache here on purpose: SFCC caching is opt-in, and an iscache tag
    inside an included template applies to the ENCLOSING page.

    Design: specs/01-widget-xss-and-enable-pref.md, sections 5.0 to 5.2.
</iscomment>
<isif condition="${pdict.gameballWidget && pdict.gameballWidget.render}">
    <div id="gameball-widget-config" data-gameball-config="${pdict.gameballWidget.configJson}" hidden></div>
    <script defer src="${URLUtils.staticURL('/js/gameballWidget.js')}"></script>
</isif>
